From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:43:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple_tristar_charger: Support the D2089

The iPad mini 2's D2089 is the iPad Air's PMIC. thisiscamk's iPad Air
(J72) measurements first established two of its charger registers: the
input-current limit at 0x4c0, with the D2365's encoding (iBoot and a
cable removal leave 0x02, 100 mA), and the charger state at 0x62 (0x42
with a source attached, 0x00 without one).

iOS 12.5.8 AppleD2089PMU (J85 kernelcache) drives the rest as
AppleD2207PMU drives the D2207, at the same addresses:

  connection state  0x60   bit 0 connected, bit 3 a new connection
  ADC               0x500  start with 0x80 | channel; done on PMU event
                           89; 12-bit result at 0x502 with the D2207's
                           byte order; afterwards 0x501 &= 7 and the
                           start bit cleared in 0x500 (_readADCGated)
  plug event        0      (AppleD2089PMUPowerSource's event bitmap)

Channel 6 is the Tristar's BrickID line, with the same millivolt scale.
So the D2089 gets the D2207's match data, and identifies sources the same
way: BC1.2, Apple BrickID, USB-C current advertisement, or the USB host's
allowance.

The board's ADT allows 2400 mA of input. On the iPad mini 2 a CDP and a
USB-C source drew the 1500 mA they advertise; nothing higher has been
measured on a D2089. Add a per-PMIC maximum, which the board maximum
cannot exceed, and hold the D2089 to 1500 mA.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
index f2c11557c..8f9dc97b3 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 /*
  * Lightning charging for Apple devices with a Tristar (CBTL1610) port
- * controller and a D2365-family PMIC (D2365, or the iPad Air 2's D2207).
+ * controller and a D2365-family PMIC (D2365, the iPad Air 2's D2207, or the
+ * iPad mini 2's D2089).
  *
  * iBoot leaves the PMIC input-current limit at 100 mA. On every attachment
  * this driver identifies the source and grants what it advertises, up to the
@@ -76,6 +77,8 @@ struct tristar_pmic {
 	u8 adc_result;		/* ADC bank: two result bytes */
 	bool adc_rearm;		/* clear the start bit and latch after a read */
 	unsigned int plug_event; /* the event that latches on plug and unplug */
+	/* The highest input limit qualified on this PMIC, in mA; 0: the board's */
+	unsigned int max_ma;
 };
 
 /* D2365 (iPad 5, iPad 6), from iOS 16 AppleD2365PMUPowerSource */
@@ -107,6 +110,25 @@ static const struct tristar_pmic tristar_d2207 = {
 	.plug_event = 0,
 };
 
+/*
+ * D2089 (iPad Air, iPad mini 2): iOS 12.5.8 AppleD2089PMU drives it as the
+ * D2207, at the same addresses, with ADC completion on event 89 and the
+ * same channel 6 scale. The iPad mini 2 drew 1500 mA from a CDP and a
+ * USB-C source; nothing above that has been measured on a D2089, so a grant
+ * stays within it whatever the board allows.
+ */
+static const struct tristar_pmic tristar_d2089 = {
+	.connected = 0x00,
+	.connected_new = BIT(3),
+	.status = 0x02,
+	.input_limit = 0x00,
+	.adc_start = TRISTAR_CHG_ADC_START | 6,
+	.adc_result = 0x02,
+	.adc_rearm = true,
+	.plug_event = 0,
+	.max_ma = 1500,
+};
+
 /* Interrupts: the PMU line, ADC completion, then the source-change events. */
 #define TRISTAR_IRQ_LINE		0
 #define TRISTAR_IRQ_ADC			1
@@ -1553,6 +1575,11 @@ static int tristar_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "missing board input-current maximum\n");
 	chg->max_ma = max_ua / 1000;
+	if (chg->pmic->max_ma && chg->max_ma > chg->pmic->max_ma) {
+		dev_info(dev, "board allows %u mA; this PMIC is qualified to %u mA\n",
+			 chg->max_ma, chg->pmic->max_ma);
+		chg->max_ma = chg->pmic->max_ma;
+	}
 
 	np = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node, "apple,tristar", 0);
 	if (!np)
@@ -1769,6 +1796,7 @@ static const struct dev_pm_ops tristar_pm_ops = {
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id tristar_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "apple,d2089-tristar-charger", .data = &tristar_d2089 },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,d2207-tristar-charger", .data = &tristar_d2207 },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,tristar-charger", .data = &tristar_d2365 },
 	{ }
